// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The Reyes family, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-06-30: two earners and a child. Two employers with plans, then a job change on
// 06-01; both 401(k)s with matches, an HSA, a dependent-care FSA, a 529, a mortgage with escrow, a credit card.
//
// This is examples/05-family after v5, so that its `accounts.ax` can be read side by side with this file. The point of
// the file is the ASSOCIATIONS: who owns what, who sponsors it, who it is for, what it implies. See ASSOCIATIONS.md §7
// for every declaration of the v4 file next to its replacement.
//
//   ✗ cannot say     ✎ says it badly     ? unclear     ⇄ what sync would need     ▸ derived, never typed
// Ids: hh-c03 is household, c = cannot say, 03; [A3] is the change in REPORT.md that closes it.
// Numbers: pay and loan terms are those of examples/05-family/contracts.ax; the mortgage and car-loan schedules are
// computed (ACTUS annuity, 30/360); every month-end balance is a replay of the lines below. Jordan's new pay and the
// supplemental rates are approximations.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

base USD
use std
use us/ca
use us/payroll
use us/401k
use us/529
use us/hsa
use us/fsa                 // a sketch: dependent-care FSA (FINDINGS 02a1)

// ── people ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// The household files one joint return. `members` is a slot of `household` (person, some); `dependents` another (person,
/// many). The v4 lines `member family` on every person and `children 1` on the household are gone: each person's side is
/// the same slot read backwards, and `children` is derived from `dependents` and `born` on the day it is read.
entity family : household
  members     alex, jordan
  dependents  riley                 // ✗ hh-c01 [A12] `children` is a count that does not age in v4; a dependent under 17 on the last day of the year is a phase of `born`
  filing      joint
  lives       us/ca

entity alex : person                // `me`
  born 1988-02-10
entity jordan : person
  born 1987-06-21
entity riley : person
  born 2019-08-22

// ── employers, and the plans they offer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A plan is a thing nested under its sponsor: the nesting fills `sponsor`, the kind-name stands for the name.

entity acme : employer
  401k-plan
    custodian fidelity
    match 40% to 10%                // 40% of what is deferred, deferrals counted up to 10% of pay
  hdhp : health-plan
    insurer blue-shield
    premium 212.50 USD per paycheck, pre-tax
    tier family                     // covers the employee and `dependents` of the household
  dcfsa : dependent-care-plan
    administrator benefit-admin
    limit 5_000 USD yearly
entity bluefin : employer
  401k-plan
    custodian fidelity
    match 50% to 6%
    vests 20% per year of service   // ✗ hh-c03 [A3] a schedule: the plan's, read when the membership ends
entity pinnacle : employer
  401k-plan
    custodian fidelity
    match 100% to 4%
    waits 60d                       // eligibility: deferrals and the match start 60 days after the employment

// ── what each person does for whom: relators, not properties ───────────────────────────────────────

/// A paycheck is one line. Withholding, FICA, SDI, the deferral, the match, the HSA, the FSA and the premium come from
/// the employment and from what it joins; they are never written.
contract alex-pay : employment with acme
  employee alex
  5_750.00 USD semi-monthly on 15, last into family/checking
  joins 401k-plan   deferral 10%    // a membership: plan, participant, election. The match is the plan's; the account is alex/401k
  joins hdhp                        // coverage: the premium, and what makes the HSA contributable
  joins dcfsa       5_000.00 USD yearly
  -> alex/hsa 250.00 USD            // a payroll contribution
contract jordan-bluefin : employment with bluefin
  employee jordan
  3_803.08 USD every 2w on friday into family/checking from 2026-01-02
  joins 401k-plan   deferral 6%
// 2026-06-01: `jordan works at pinnacle` starts the next one (see the journal)

// ── where the money sits: positions under their institution, named by the people they relate ─────────
// `alex/401k` is alex's 401(k) with fidelity: `alex` fills `owner`, `fidelity` (the nesting) fills `with`, and the kind is
// the last word. No name carries a relation; `jordan-401k` and `riley-529` are not needed.

entity chase : bank
  family/checking   : deposit
  family/savings    : deposit
    interest 3.95% on the daily balance, paid monthly       // ✗ hh-c05 [A7] a term of the position; v4 types each month's interest as a line
  family/card       : credit-card
    in full monthly on 25 from checking
entity fidelity : broker
  alex/401k                         // sponsor: alex's employer on the day it opens (acme), by the default of kind 401k  ? hh-u11 [A2] a default is a guess about the past
  jordan/bluefin/401k               // a second one will exist: the path names the sponsor so the two are told apart
  alex/hsa
    coverage family                 // ? hh-u07 [A1] a closed enum here; it should be what alex's `hdhp` covers, and nothing says the HSA needs that coverage
  family/529
    beneficiary riley               // `family` fills `owner` (a household), `riley` the only unfilled slot a person can fill
entity benefit-admin : plan-administrator
  alex/dcfsa
    sponsor acme                    // by default: alex's employer
    dependents riley
entity rocket : lender
  family/mortgage : loan 406_692.02 USD on 2025-12-31 at 5.875% over 27y6m for house
    monthly on 1 from checking
    also -> escrow 705.00 USD #escrow        // `escrow` is a position the kind `mortgage` implies: family's, with rocket
entity honda-finance : lender
  family/car-loan : loan 16_976.91 USD on 2025-12-31 at 4.9% over 30m for crv
    monthly on 5 from checking

asset house : home
  owner family
asset crv : vehicle
  owner family

// ── who else ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity blue-shield : health-insurer
entity county : government
entity homeguard, statefarm : insurer
entity costco, trader-joes : grocer
entity target, amazon : store
entity shell : fuel
entity pge, comcast, verizon : utility
entity netflix : streaming
entity little-sprouts : childcare-provider
entity st-annes-school : school
entity smile-dental : medical-provider
entity irs, ftb, ssa, edd : tax-authority

