// ═════ what the checker says when an association is wrong (each is an error; the fix is an edit) ═════════
//
//   error[ambiguous-role]: `riley` can fill two roles of this 529: `owner` and `beneficiary`
//      family/529                                   (the household `family` fills `owner`, so `riley` can only be `beneficiary`: accepted)
//      riley/529                                    (nothing else fills a slot: `riley` could own it or be its beneficiary)
//   = help: write the role: `beneficiary riley`
//
//   error[wrong-kind]: `beneficiary acme`: acme is an employer, and a 529's `beneficiary` is a person
//   = help: did you mean `beneficiary riley`?
//
//   error[missing-role]: alex/hsa has no `coverage`: the kind `hsa` needs one of `self-only | family`
//   = help: coverage family
//
//   error[too-many]: family/529 has two `beneficiary`: riley, jordan (a 529 has one)
//   = help: open a second 529, or `beneficiary riley` only
//
//   warning[former-employer]: jordan/bluefin/401k has no employment behind it since 05-29: no match, no new deferrals
//   note: this is what a former-employer account is; it is not an error
//
// ═════ index of marks ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   hh-b06  ✎     [A3]     a final pay (accrued PTO, supplemental withholding) is a rule of the employment's end
//   hh-c01  ✗     [A12]    `children` and `member` as properties: dependents are a slot of the household and being under 17 is a phase of `born`, read on the day
//   hh-c03  ✗     [A3]     vesting: a schedule of the plan, triggered when the employment ends (forfeiture of the unvested match)
//   hh-c04  ✗     [A3]     plan eligibility: a waiting period that is a term of the plan, read by the membership
//   hh-c05  ✗     [A7]     interest on a balance (savings, a card, a line) as a term of the position, not a typed line each month
//   hh-s08  ⇄     [sync]   paystubs: print `15 alex-pay` when the stub is the contract's, its legs when it is not
//   hh-s09  ⇄     [sync]   the servicer's annual escrow analysis as a `now` statement on the escrow term
//   hh-s10  ⇄     [sync]   the 529 and HSA custodians' statements, with the plan's own claim numbers as codes
//   hh-u07  ?     [A1]     HSA coverage as a closed enum vs what the HDHP actually covers; HSA eligibility needs that coverage and nobody else's
//   hh-u11  ?     [A2]     a default for `sponsor` is a guess about the past: an account that predates the book must say who sponsored it
